  "correction_rules": [
    "Overall bias: model is slightly high vs realized, especially in the back half of the horizon (roughly days 15–30). Apply a small downward level shift that increases with horizon (near-zero in week 1, larger by weeks 3–4).",
    "Peak/overshoot behavior: after upward moves in history, the model tends to project too-strong continuation and overshoots local highs by ~0.3–1.5. Damp positive momentum signals; cap daily gains and pull forecasts toward the recent 10–15d mean when forecast exceeds that mean by >~1.",
    "Mean-reversion underweighting: true series reverts faster than the model implies. Increase mean-reversion strength so deviations from the 2–3 week average decay more quickly (notably mid-horizon).",
    "Late-horizon drawdown error: the model often drops too far in the final week when it starts forecasting a decline (e.g., predicts low 60s while realized rebounds to mid/high 60s). Reduce negative momentum extrapolation beyond ~day 20; impose a floor anchored to the recent 20–30d range/mean.",
    "Volatility smoothing: model path is too smooth and trend-like; realized has more short-term oscillation around a level. Add mild re-centering each step toward a rolling mean to avoid persistent drift."
  ]
}
